*> Declarative procedures can run before any statement of the program,
*> so what they set is not reported as used before it is set. ERRORS
*> is still reported: nothing sets it before the ADD.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. DECLS.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT IN-FILE ASSIGN TO "INPUT"
        FILE STATUS IS IN-STATUS.
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD  IN-FILE.
01  IN-REC          PIC X(80).
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  IN-STATUS       PIC XX.
01  LAST-ERROR      PIC XX.
01  ERRORS          PIC 9(4).
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
DECLARATIVES.
IO-ERRORS SECTION.
    USE AFTER STANDARD ERROR PROCEDURE ON IN-FILE.
NOTE-ERROR.
    MOVE IN-STATUS TO LAST-ERROR.
END DECLARATIVES.
MAIN SECTION.
MAIN-LINE.
    OPEN INPUT IN-FILE
    DISPLAY LAST-ERROR
    ADD 1 TO ERRORS
    MOVE 0 TO ERRORS
    CLOSE IN-FILE
    STOP RUN.
